# Git rewrites LF to CRLF on Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf, the default on
# GitHub's windows runners). For anything compared byte for byte that is
# corruption, not a formatting difference — a DER timestamp token gains a 0x0D
# before every 0x0A, its declared ASN.1 lengths stop matching the buffer, and
# parsing fails with an error that says nothing about line endings. Verified:
# response.tsr goes 2624 -> 2643 bytes and parseTimeStampResponse throws.
#
# So: every fixture whose exact bytes matter is marked -text.

# RFC 3161 requests, responses and DER blobs
*.tsr   -text
*.tsq   -text
*.der   -text
*.bin   -text

# Keys and certificates — parsed strictly, and hashed in places
*.pem   -text

# Evidence exports and stores, verified against a recorded hash
*.tgev  -text
*.sqlite -text

# The TSA fixture corpus: nonces and JSON here are diffed against recomputed
# values, so keep the whole directory byte-exact rather than listing types.
packages/cli/test-fixtures/** -text

# Frozen canonicalization vectors — the point of them is byte equality.
docs/test-vectors/** -text
